@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About | It's a Budget</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Learn why It's a Budget takes a practical, checkbook-first approach to household money." />
</HeadContent>

<article class="public-page">
    <p class="public-page-kicker">ABOUT</p>
    <h1>Money planning for real life</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        It's a Budget is a checkbook-first household budgeting application built
        to answer a practical question: what will the balance look like after the
        bills and income ahead?
    </p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
        Budgets are most useful when they connect day-to-day transactions with
        the plan ahead. It's a Budget combines a running ledger, recurring
        budget items, forecasts, category allowances, reminders, reports, and
        optional bank connections in one focused place.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
        You remain in control of the checkbook. Connected-bank data is staged
        for review, and suggested matches do not silently rewrite your ledger.
        Shared budgets use explicit memberships and roles so household access
        can be managed deliberately.
    </p>

    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <p>
        It's a Budget is a planning and recordkeeping tool. It is not a bank,
        lender, investment adviser, tax adviser, or credit-repair service.
    </p>

    <div class="public-callout">
        <h2>Ready to continue?</h2>
        <p>Existing users can sign in to their private budget.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-brand" href="/login">Sign in securely</a>
    </div>
</article>
